# Read by `dart pub publish` INSTEAD of the .gitignore in this directory, and
# that substitution is the whole reason the file exists.
#
# Everything here is build output the repository deliberately does not track
# (scripts/build-runtime.sh platform=web writes it), and pub publishes nothing
# git ignores -- so without this file the published ssplayer_flutter carries an
# EMPTY assets/runtime-web/, and every web consumer's loader (ssruntime_dart's
# web_runtime.dart, which asks for these three files by name) finds nothing.
# Nothing fails at build time; the animation simply never starts.
#
# Having no rules is most of the point: replacing this directory's .gitignore is
# what re-includes the two .wasm. The one negation below is for the
# repository-root .gitignore's `*.js`, which a .pubignore HERE does not replace
# and which would otherwise still hide the wasm-bindgen glue.
#
# The flip side is that pub packs what is on DISK: the web runtime has to be
# built before publishing. scripts/build-release.sh fails the release when the
# archive comes out without it.
!ssruntime.js
